      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "What are the standard free energy change and the equilibrium constant for the following reaction at 25 °C?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "fpef2e2m9iznosr",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "ckmshx1c00rf0y9",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xqucbtlw39hmati",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "2\\;\\mathrm{Ag}^+(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{Fe}(s)\\;\\;\\rightarrow\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{Ag}(s)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}(aq)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "This is an oxidation-reduction reaction, so the standard cell potential can be calculated using the data found in the "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Standard Reduction Potentials"
                      }
                    ],
                    "href": "/course/link/iz1ln_standard_reduction_potentials_mv70v",
                    "idref": "80874",
                    "target": "new",
                    "type": "a"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " table."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "05v53bxhoovwx9h",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "qmjjfidk6tfgtup",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "g80ovlysked8yos",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{l}\\mathrm{Anode}\\;(\\mathrm{oxidation}):\\mathrm{Fe}(s)\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}(aq)\\;+\\;2\\;\\mathrm e^-\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;E_{\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}/\\mathrm{Fe}}^\\circ\\;=\\;-0.447\\;\\mathrm V\\\\\\mathrm{Cathode}\\;(\\mathrm{reduction}):\\;2\\;\\times\\;(\\mathrm{Ag}^+(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm e^-\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;\\mathrm{Ag}(s))\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;E_{\\mathrm{Ag}^+/\\mathrm{Ag}}^\\circ\\;=\\;0.7996\\;\\mathrm V\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "5i071k7zfr4e1ys",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "iukcq4o8te2v6rb",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{l}E_{\\mathrm{cell}}^\\circ\\;=\\;E_{\\mathrm{cathode}}^\\circ\\; -\\;E_{\\mathrm{anode}}^\\circ\\;\\\\E_{\\mathrm{Ag}^+/\\mathrm{Ag}}^\\circ\\; -\\;E_{\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}/\\mathrm{Fe}}^\\circ\\;=\\;+1.247\\;\\;\\mathrm V\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Remember that the cell potential for the cathode is not multiplied by two when determining the standard cell potential. Using "
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "n"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " = 2, the equilibrium constant is calculated:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "uhzaiit2h25x7d2",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "7y7ad18xp2wy0b0",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "5w2itarec406zno",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{l}E_{\\mathrm{cell}}^{\\circ}\\;=\\;\\frac{\\;0.0592\\;\\mathrm{V}}{n\\;}\\log K\\;\\;\\;\\;\\Rightarrow\\;\\;\\;\\; K\\;=\\;10^{(nE_\\mathrm{cell}^\\circ/0.0592\\;\\mathrm{V})}\\\\K\\;=\\;10^{(2\\times1.247\\;\\mathrm{V}/0.0592\\;\\mathrm{V})\\;}\\;=\\;10^{42.128}\\; =\\;1.3\\times10^{42}\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The standard free energy is then:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "tjt9pg38vc0jogk",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "9umfr12fft8wg8u",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "rp6zfhgsks30sce",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm\\Delta G^\\circ=-nF{E_\\mathrm{cell}^\\circ}\\;=\\;-\\left(2\\;\\mathrm{mol}\\right)\\; \\left(96,485\\;\\mathrm J/\\mathrm V\\cdot\\mathrm{mol}\\;\\right)\\left(1.247\\;\\mathrm V\\right)\\; =\\;-240.6\\;\\mathrm{kJ}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Check your answer: A positive standard cell potential means a spontaneous reaction, so the standard free energy change should be negative, and the equilibrium constant should be >1."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "vq7hzf8wfqde57b",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
